ction. The most recent production release marked healthy is v2.3.0, so I rolled back to it in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted with a partial failure after us-east (orchestrator error), leaving the fleet mixed. I retried the rollback, and it completed: all three regions are on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: investigate the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging), investigate the orchestrator partial failure, and confirm checkout traffic and error rates are stable.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out. I'll check whether it was created before retrying, so I don't open a duplicate page.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01VewprcQ9CZcpKv8647L4Qo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was the latest release and was unhealthy in production. v2.3.0 was the most recent production release marked healthy. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the fleet mixed. Retrying the same rollback completed it. No change-manager approval was needed, since v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as SEV2 for checkout-api. The create call timed out, but when I listed incidents it was already there, so I did not open a duplicate. The summary covers the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and follow-ups.\n\nFollow-ups for the team: find out why v2.3.1 failed (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging), look into the orchestrator partial failure, and confirm checkout traffic and error rates stay stable.", "type": "text"}]}]}